aquinas-st-i-3.logic.r2: argue/scope: A1: read with the necessity on its consequent alone, will_inclination → □(according_will → ¬against_incl), the argument holds; read with it on the whole conditional, □(will_inclination → (according_will → ¬against_incl)), C (S5) does not follow: it needs the necessity of the consequent, not only of the consequence, and which the sentence means decides the argument
